        The root cause of the bug is the continued support for the deprecated `dfs.umask` configuration, which led to confusion and potential misconfiguration. Users could inadvertently rely on the old configuration key, causing inconsistencies in permission settings and unexpected behavior in file system operations. The code was designed to handle both the old and new configuration keys, but this dual support created complexity and the risk of errors when the values did not match.

        Commit message:
        HADOOP-12294. Remove the support of the deprecated dfs.umask.
